    "title": "Chapter 7",
    "start_page": 50,
    "end_page": 53,
    "pages": [
      {
        "page_number": 50,
        "elements": []
      },
      {
        "page_number": 51,
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12279",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              48.01917266845703,
              79.0199966430664,
              57.01917266845703
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The use of automation comes with certain cautions. Automation should reduce workload, but in some instances, it may create ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              58.087425231933594,
              560.51611328125,
              68.0874252319336
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "more work, confusion, and contribute to errors. At other times, automation may lull pilots into complacency. Pilots who ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              69.0874252319336,
              560.5230102539062,
              79.0874252319336
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "consistently rely on an autopilot for flight path management may experience degraded ability to fly manually when required ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              80.0874252319336,
              560.513916015625,
              90.0874252319336
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "to do so. For example, when flying in icing conditions, an automated system may make control inputs to compensate for ice ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              91.0874252319336,
              560.4852294921875,
              101.0874252319336
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "accumulation. However, if the system exceeds its limits, it could disconnect and leave the aircraft in an undesired state. A pilot ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              102.0874252319336,
              560.4863891601562,
              112.0874252319336
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "who has become unaccustomed to manual flight may not be prepared to handle the situation.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              113.0874252319336,
              424.780029296875,
              123.0874252319336
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12290",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              124.81916046142578,
              79.0199966430664,
              133.8191680908203
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Reprogramming tasks that occur unexpectedly can trigger pilot errors, which may result in flight path deviations or other ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              134.88742065429688,
              560.529052734375,
              144.88742065429688
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "undesired aircraft states. Pilots should anticipate the need to fly manually and be prepared to maintain the desired flight path ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              145.88742065429688,
              560.5040283203125,
              155.88742065429688
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "when manual control becomes necessary.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              156.88742065429688,
              219.1220245361328,
              166.88742065429688
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12287",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              168.6192169189453,
              79.0199966430664,
              177.6192169189453
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pilots who use automation should train and practice for various scenarios in order to avoid becoming overly distracted when ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              178.68746948242188,
              560.47802734375,
              188.68746948242188
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "making a programming change or correcting an error. Being startled or confused by a programming mistake or automation ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              189.68746948242188,
              560.5220336914062,
              199.68746948242188
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "malfunction occurs less often when the pilot has the capability for transition to manual flight. If the automation is not functioning ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              200.68746948242188,
              560.5198364257812,
              210.68746948242188
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "according to expectation, the pilot may reduce the level of automation, fly manually, and take time to resolve the condition.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              211.68746948242188,
              547.3870849609375,
              221.68746948242188
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Balancing Automated & Manual Flight",
            "font_name": "Arial-BoldMT",
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "color": "#AA1E22",
            "is_bold": true,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              240.29660034179688,
              251.6094207763672,
              251.29660034179688
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12291",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              252.41920471191406,
              79.0199966430664,
              261.419189453125
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pilots choose the level of flight path automation. Risk management strategies suggest using automation as an aid to manage ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              262.4874572753906,
              560.5045166015625,
              272.4874572753906
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "workload rather than to compensate for lack of proficiency. A balance of automated and manual flight that takes workload and ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              273.4874572753906,
              560.5191040039062,
              283.4874572753906
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "proficiency into consideration gives the pilot greater opportunity to monitor the flight path and aircraft state.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              284.4874572753906,
              487.2799377441406,
              294.4874572753906
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12291-2",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              296.21917724609375,
              87.02099609375,
              305.21917724609375
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Choosing the appropriate level of automation for the task and adjusting as circumstances dictate is essential to effective use of ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              306.2874450683594,
              560.5142211914062,
              316.2874450683594
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "automation.  One of the most common errors is failing to move to lower levels of automation suitable to a changing environment.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              317.2874450683594,
              558.0330200195312,
              327.2874450683594
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12292",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              329.0191650390625,
              79.0199966430664,
              338.0191650390625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "For example, a pilot may track an approach course adequately using manual control inputs. However, the pilot may also need to ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              339.0874328613281,
              560.5331420898438,
              349.0874328613281
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "listen to and record the Automatic Terminal Information Service (ATIS), retrieve and load an instrument approach procedure, ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              350.0874328613281,
              560.5121459960938,
              360.0874328613281
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "prepare for the instrument approach, and accomplish the appropriate checklists. These tasks will increase workload and divert ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              361.0874328613281,
              560.4971313476562,
              371.0874328613281
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "pilot attention from monitoring and controlling the flight path. If using an autopilot to track the approach, the automation ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              372.0874328613281,
              560.5099487304688,
              382.0874328613281
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "performs the control inputs and allows the pilot to complete other tasks quickly and efficiently.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              383.0874328613281,
              433.35498046875,
              393.0874328613281
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12293",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              394.8191833496094,
              79.0199966430664,
              403.8191833496094
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Continuing the scenario above, the pilot loads the instrument approach and decides to remain on autopilot. However, after the ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              404.887451171875,
              560.5150756835938,
              414.887451171875
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "aircraft passes the initial approach fix, ATC cancels the approach clearance. ATC provides vectors and tells the pilot to expect ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              415.887451171875,
              560.5286865234375,
              425.887451171875
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "to hold. In this situation, the pilot may select basic autopilot modes that control heading and altitude in order to comply with the ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              426.887451171875,
              560.5090942382812,
              436.887451171875
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "assignment from ATC. The lower level of automation allows the pilot to program and configure the aircraft for an unexpected ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              437.887451171875,
              560.5148315429688,
              447.887451171875
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "change while keeping the flightpath and aircraft state under control.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              448.887451171875,
              325.04998779296875,
              458.887451171875
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12295",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              460.6191711425781,
              79.0199966430664,
              469.6191711425781
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Pilots may sometimes choose to disengage the automation and fly the aircraft manually to maintain proficiency.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              470.68743896484375,
              501.0069580078125,
              480.68743896484375
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Interacting with Automation",
            "font_name": "Arial-BoldMT",
            "font_size": 11.0,
            "color": "#AA1E22",
            "is_bold": true,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              499.29656982421875,
              199.03384399414062,
              510.29656982421875
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12296",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              511.419189453125,
              79.0199966430664,
              520.419189453125
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Regardless of the level of automation, pilots should consider the following series of steps: [",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              521.4874267578125,
              419.8000183105469,
              531.4874267578125
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12297",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              533.2191772460938,
              79.0199966430664,
              542.2191772460938
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "1.\t Anticipate – Understand the system well enough to know what should happen before pushing a button or turning a ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              67.0,
              543.2874145507812,
              541.780029296875,
              553.2874145507812
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "knob.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              81.0,
              554.2874145507812,
              103.5,
              564.2874145507812
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12298",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              566.0191650390625,
              79.0199966430664,
              575.0191650390625
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "2.\t Act – Execute button pushes and knob turns to implement the desired automation.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              67.0,
              576.08740234375,
              409.030029296875,
              586.08740234375
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12299",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              587.8191528320312,
              79.0199966430664,
              596.8191528320312
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "3.\t Verify – Ensure the aircraft or avionics performs as expected.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              67.0,
              597.8873901367188,
              326.4830627441406,
              607.8873901367188
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "]",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              462.4375,
              521.4874267578125,
              465.7674865722656,
              531.4874267578125
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Figure 7-2",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPS-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              419.7616882324219,
              521.5166015625,
              462.4386901855469,
              531.5166015625
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "page_number": 52,
        "elements": []
      },
      {
        "page_number": 53,
        "elements": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "autopilot systems with ease and in a routine manner.",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              46.212730407714844,
              263.1209716796875,
              56.21273422241211
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "12309",
            "font_name": "Arial-ItalicMT",
            "font_size": 9.0,
            "color": "#FFFFFF",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": true,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              57.94446563720703,
              79.0199966430664,
              66.94446563720703
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Knowledge of system limitations and operating restrictions is also important. Pilots should know emergency procedures pertaining ",
            "font_name": "TimesNewRomanPSMT",
            "font_size": 10.0,
            "color": "#000000",
            "is_bold": false,
            "is_italic": false,
            "bbox": [
              54.0,
              68.0127182006836,
              560.522216796875,
              78.0127182006836
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
